 "mechanism": {
  "change": "divRemAlloc hands divRemAbsAlloc borrowed sign-cleared views of the caller's limbs instead of two absCloneWithAllocator copies",
  "why_it_is_safe": "nothing writes through either operand: the lhs < rhs arm clones, the single-limb arm only reads, and the long division copies both into its own u and v scratch before touching anything",
  "guard": "the OOM sweep already asserts the caller's operand limbs are byte-for-byte unchanged after every injected failure, so a future write would fail there rather than silently corrupt a caller's BigInt",
